     or brightness keys will not work.
  2. Drop your dotfiles into ~/.config/sway and ~/.config/kitty.
     Make sure your sway config has:  include ~/.config/sway/config.d/*
     Otherwise the portal environment drop-in is ignored.
  3. Start with:  ~/.local/bin/start-sway
     Do NOT just run `sway` — the wrapper is what loads the session env.
     (or re-run this script with --tty-autostart)
  4. Point your configs at the Nerd Fonts this script installed:
       kitty:   font_family FiraCode Nerd Font
       waybar:  font-family: "FiraCode Nerd Font", "Symbols Nerd Font Mono";
     The Symbols face is glyphs only — it is the fontconfig fallback that
     makes icons work in any font, so keep it last in the list.

Verify it worked:
  echo $XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP          # must print: sway
  brightnessctl s 50%                # must not say "permission denied"
  wpctl status                       # pipewire should list your card
  /usr/libexec/xdg-desktop-portal -r # restart portals if sharing misbehaves

  `sudo fwupdmgr refresh && sudo fwupdmgr update` — do this early, Lenovo
  ships real firmware fixes for the T14 Gen 3 through LVFS.

EOF
